	abstract = {Accurate and automatic segmentation of medical images is a crucial step for clinical diagnosis and analysis. The convolutional neural network (CNN) approaches based on the U-shape structure have achieved remarkable performances in many different medical image segmentation tasks. However, the context information extraction capability of single stage is insufficient in this structure, due to the problems such as imbalanced class and blurredboundary. In thispaper,we proposea novel Context Pyramid FusionNetwork (named CPFNet) by combining two pyramidal modules to fuse global/multi-scale context information.Based on the U-shape structure,we first design multiple global pyramid guidance (GPG) modules between the encoder and the decoder, aiming at providing different levels of global context information for the decoder by reconstructing skip-connection.We further design a scaleaware pyramid fusion (SAPF) module to dynamically fuse multi-scale context information in high-level features. These two pyramidal modules can exploit and fuse rich context information progressively. Experimental results show that our proposed method is very competitive with other state-of-the-artmethods on four different challenging tasks, including skin lesionsegmentation, retinal linear lesion segmentation, multi-class segmentation of thoracic organs at risk and multi-class segmentation of retinal edema lesions. © 2020 Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.. All rights reserved.},
